---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<!--
	Variant 9 — "Letter"
	One long-form page written in first person, like a letter or a Sivers-style
	about page. No cards, no grid — just prose with generous type, broken by
	thin rules and small glyph marks. The most personal of the set: it reads
	like the person, not the résumé.
-->
<BaseLayout
	title="Tarik Duyar — About"
	description="Ahmet Tarik Duyar — software engineer in Sarajevo. Who I am, what I build, what I care about."
	bodyClass="bg-[#0b0c0f] text-gray-300 antialiased"
>
	<main class="max-w-xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-32">
		<!-- Opening -->
		<header class="mb-16">
			<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-400/40 text-2xl block mb-8 select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐱅</span>
			<h1 class="font-sinistre text-4xl md:text-5xl text-white leading-tight mb-2">
				I'm Tarik.
			</h1>
			<p class="text-gray-500">Software engineer. Sarajevo.</p>
		</header>

		<div class="space-y-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed text-[17px]">
			<p>
				I build software for a living and, inconveniently for my free time, also
				for fun.
			</p>
			<p>
				The living part: since 2022 I've been the engineer behind
				<span class="text-white">EgeceTV</span>, a streaming platform at Deniz
				Egece with more than 17,000 paying subscribers across five platforms.
				I designed its backend, its database, its payment system, and the
				pipeline that deploys it. When something breaks at 2am, my phone is the
				one that buzzes — which has taught me more about software design than
				any book.
			</p>
			<p>
				The fun part happens below the web stack. I'm writing
				<a href="https://github.com/atduyar/rekv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors underline decoration-blue-400/30 underline-offset-4">a key-value store in Rust</a>
				to understand how storage engines actually work, and before that I built
				<a href="https://github.com/atduyar/make2game" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors underline decoration-blue-400/30 underline-offset-4">a 2D game engine in C++</a>
				to understand what Unity was hiding from me. Neither will take over the
				world. Both rewired how I think.
			</p>
		</div>

		<hr class="my-12 border-white/5" />

		<div class="space-y-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed text-[17px]">
			<p class="text-gray-500 text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">What I believe about software</p>
			<p>
				Boring architecture wins. The most valuable systems I've shipped were the
				least clever ones — a single well-designed API serving five client
				platforms beats five special snowflakes every time.
			</p>
			<p>
				Owning the whole stack changes how you build. I run my own servers — this
				site, a Matrix homeserver, the projects I host. Self-hosting is mostly a
				hobby, but it keeps me honest: you write different code when you're also
				the one operating it.
			</p>
			<p>
				And you should regularly build one layer below where you work. The web
				made sense to me only after I wrote the renderer; databases made sense
				only once I memory-mapped a file myself.
			</p>
		</div>

		<hr class="my-12 border-white/5" />

		<div class="space-y-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed text-[17px]">
			<p class="text-gray-500 text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Right now</p>
			<p>
				Finishing my computer science degree at the International University of
				Sarajevo (as an honor student, my mother would want you to know),
				shipping at Deniz Egece, and slowly turning my drafts about Matrix
				federation and Rust ownership into an actual blog. It will appear here
				when it's ready.
			</p>
			<p>
				The glyphs on this page are <span class="text-white">Old Turkic</span> —
				an alphabet carved into stone in the Orkhon Valley thirteen centuries
				ago. I keep them around as a reminder that good engineering outlives its
				engineers: those inscriptions are still readable; most software doesn't
				survive a decade.
			</p>
		</div>

		<hr class="my-12 border-white/5" />

		<!-- Sign-off -->
		<footer>
			<p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed text-[17px] mb-10">
				If any of this resonates — about work, side projects, or an argument
				over whether self-hosting email is ever worth it — write to me at
				<a href="mailto:atduyar@gmail.com" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors underline decoration-blue-400/30 underline-offset-4">atduyar@gmail.com</a>.
			</p>
			<div class="flex items-center justify-between">
				<div class="flex gap-5 text-sm text-gray-500">
					<a href="https://github.com/atduyar" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">GitHub</a>
					<a href="https://linkedin.com/in/atduyar" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">LinkedIn</a>
				</div>
				<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-400/25 text-lg tracking-[0.3em] select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐰋𐰃𐰠𐰏</span>
			</div>
			<p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-10">© 2026 Ahmet Tarik Duyar</p>
		</footer>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>
